- Authoritative pytest commands MUST show tests EXECUTED (e.g., "19 passed", explicit failures)
- "no tests ran" output is AUTOMATIC FAIL regardless of collection count
- Chat output MUST be limited to: evidence file path + commit hash + STOP

Hard violation cases (IMMEDIATE FAIL):
- Evidence not captured via Tee-Object (2>&1)
- pytest output shows "no tests ran" 
- Multiple evidence files per phase
- Chat includes narrative beyond required outputs

## -3. Wave/Phase Budget Lock (ANTI-INFINITE LOOP)
Maximum execution budgets to prevent spin:

Per phase:
- Each wave MUST have evidence capture
- Phase MUST complete with proper evidence documentation

Per plan:
- Plans should be reasonably scoped to maintain focus
- Split large plans when they become unwieldy

Hard violation cases (IMMEDIATE FAIL):
- Continuing without phase completion evidence
- Excessively long-running phases without documentation

